    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_2",
      "quote": "To improve older patients' physical activity (PA) behavior, it is important to identify facilitators and barriers to enhancing PA in older patients ( ≥ 65 years) during hospitalization from the perspectives of patients, caregivers, and healthcare professionals (HCPs).",
      "reason": "The text explicitly states the importance of identifying these facilitators and barriers to improve physical activity behavior in older patients."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "The provided text does not indicate that this is an update or replication of a specific previous systematic review, nor does it mention the existence of similar reviews that necessitate an explanation for the current one."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": null,
      "quote": null,
      "reason": "This is a review of facilitators and barriers, not a review of intervention effects."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_7",
      "quote": "The adapted framework of the social ecological model [39] was therefore used, consisting of intrapersonal, interpersonal, and institutional levels (Additional file 4), which was used previously in systematic reviews [30, 31].",
      "reason": "The authors used the social ecological model as a framework to categorize the facilitators and barriers, which serves as a conceptual model for the complex context of physical activity in hospitals."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 100
